<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francisco de Paula Santander</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1792">1792</a>–<a href="/years/1840">1840</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francisco de Paula Santander was a New Granadan general of the wars of independence who fought beside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boyaca-department">Boyacá</a> in 1819. As vice-president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esztergom">Gran</a> Colombia he governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogota">Bogotá</a> while Bolívar campaigned in the south, but the two fell out, and Santander was exiled after the attempt on Bolívar's life in 1828. He returned to serve as president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/republic-of-new-granada">Republic of New Granada</a> from 1832 to 1837.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francisco-de-paula-santander.jpg" alt="Francisco de Paula Santander" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ricardo Acevedo Bernal · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Santander_by_Acevedo_Bernal.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
